  "caveats": [
    "Loopback on one physical host; server and client each get 2 physical cores, but share L3, memory, kernel network stack and IRQs.",
    "No root: no cgroups, IRQ affinity or process isolation; desktop/IDE and other agents ran during measurements; loadavg 2-10.",
    "Different storage/architecture: pulsed mmap binary store; BIND rbtdb from master files; Unbound auth-zone in memory; PowerDNS gsqlite3 (SQLite per cache miss, no preload).",
    "PDNS cache-ttl=0 is the fair no-cache auth variant; cache-ttl=60 is shown for context. pulsed response cache is a separate binary-answer cache.",
    "Shipped pulse-loadgen sends RD=0; BIND, Unbound and PowerDNS recursors answer REFUSED (verified by relay: Unbound rcode 5). Resolver phase uses a local one-line RD=1 build of the same loadgen; authoritative results were cross-checked with the shipped tool and match within noise.",
    "Open-loop p50 ~357 us is the client pacing floor of pulse-loadgen on this host, not server latency; open-loop primarily shows that 10k qps is sustained without loss.",
    "PDNS linked against OpenSSL 3.5.9 while libcurl pulls libcrypto 4 into the same process; functional but not a distro-default build.",
    "Unbound's built-in 'test.' local-zone shadows z0.bench.test.; disabled with local-zone nodefault in both Unbound configs."
  ]
}